# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Overview {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With SQOA Solver by JIJ, you can solve large combinatorial optimization problems on IBM&reg; quantum computers. The solver is based on the Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) [\\[1\\]](#references). Unlike quantum algorithms that use a one-to-one mapping between classical decision variables and qubits, SQOA Solver can handle optimization problems with more variables than the number of qubits available on current quantum devices. Its sampling-based design also makes it less sensitive to the physical noise on current quantum hardware. Together, these features make SQOA Solver well suited to optimization problems at this stage of quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang SQOA Solver ng JIJ, malulutas mo ang malalaking combinatorial optimization problem sa mga quantum computer ng IBM&reg;. Ang solver ay batay sa Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) [\\[1\\]](#references). Hindi tulad ng mga quantum algorithm na gumagamit ng one-to-one mapping sa pagitan ng classical decision variable at qubit, kaya ng SQOA Solver na humawak ng mga optimization problem na mas marami ang variable kaysa sa bilang ng qubit na available sa mga kasalukuyang quantum device. Dahil sa sampling-based na disenyo nito, mas hindi rin ito sensitibo sa physical noise ng kasalukuyang quantum hardware. Dahil sa mga katangiang ito, bagay na bagay ang SQOA Solver sa mga optimization problem sa kasalukuyang yugto ng quantum computing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solver handles Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) problems given as a classical mathematical formulation, and it automatically maps the classical formulation into the quantum setting. You can also convert constrained problems into unconstrained ones by using the penalty method.\n"
msgstr "Hinahawakan ng solver ang mga Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) problem na ibinigay bilang classical mathematical formulation, at awtomatiko nitong imamapa ang classical formulation sa quantum setting. Puwede mo ring gawing unconstrained ang mga constrained problem gamit ang penalty method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following sections describe the solver's workflow, benchmark results, and end-to-end examples that model problems with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper) and, optionally, Open Mathematical prograMming eXchange (OMMX). [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) is an open data format and SDK that simplifies the exchange of optimization problems between software tools.\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng mga sumusunod na seksyon ang workflow ng solver, mga resulta ng benchmark, at mga end-to-end na halimbawa na nagmo-model ng mga problema gamit ang [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper) at, opsyonal, ang Open Mathematical prograMming eXchange (OMMX). Ang [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) ay isang open data format at SDK na nagpapadali sa pagpapalitan ng mga optimization problem sa pagitan ng mga software tool.\n"

