# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SQOA framework {#the-sqoa-framework}"
msgstr "Ang SQOA framework {#the-sqoa-framework}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA is a sampling-based framework for combinatorial optimization [\\[1\\]](#references). It combines two techniques: Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[2\\]](#references), which encodes the problem in a quantum relaxation, and sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) [\\[3\\]](#references), also known as quantum-selected configuration interaction (QSCI) [\\[4\\]](#references), which uses the quantum computer only to sample bitstrings and finds the low-energy state on a classical computer. SQOA is a framework in the sense that it fixes this combination but leaves the details to each implementation, such as how the variables are assigned to qubits and which circuits generate the samples.\n"
msgstr "Ang SQOA ay isang sampling-based na framework para sa combinatorial optimization [\\[1\\]](#references). Pinagsasama nito ang dalawang technique: ang Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[2\\]](#references), na nag-e-encode ng problema sa isang quantum relaxation, at ang sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) [\\[3\\]](#references), na kilala rin bilang quantum-selected configuration interaction (QSCI) [\\[4\\]](#references), na gumagamit ng quantum computer para lang mag-sample ng mga bitstring at hinahanap ang low-energy state sa isang classical computer. Ang SQOA ay isang framework dahil itinatakda nito ang kombinasyong ito pero iniiwan ang mga detalye sa bawat implementasyon, tulad ng kung paano itinatalaga ang mga variable sa mga qubit at kung aling mga circuit ang gumagawa ng mga sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum relaxation with QRAO.** QAOA and other Ising-based approaches represent each binary variable by the $Z$ operator of its qubit. QRAO also uses the $X$ and $Y$ operators. With a (3,1) quantum random access code (QRAC), up to three binary variables share one qubit, and each variable is represented by a different Pauli operator.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum relaxation gamit ang QRAO.** Ang QAOA at iba pang Ising-based na approach ay kumakatawan sa bawat binary variable gamit ang $Z$ operator ng qubit nito. Gumagamit din ang QRAO ng mga $X$ at $Y$ operator. Sa (3,1) quantum random access code (QRAC), hanggang tatlong binary variable ang puwedeng magbahagi ng isang qubit, at ang bawat variable ay kinakatawan ng ibang Pauli operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The QUBO then becomes a relaxed Hamiltonian that needs fewer qubits than the Ising Hamiltonian. Variables that interact in the QUBO must be placed on different qubits. If they shared a qubit, the product of their Pauli operators would reduce to a single operator on that qubit (for example, $XY = iZ$), and the relaxed Hamiltonian would no longer represent their interaction.\n"
msgstr "  Ang QUBO ay nagiging relaxed Hamiltonian na mas kaunti ang kailangang qubit kaysa sa Ising Hamiltonian. Ang mga variable na nag-i-interact sa QUBO ay dapat ilagay sa magkakaibang qubit. Kung magbabahagi sila ng qubit, ang product ng kanilang mga Pauli operator ay magiging iisang operator na lang sa qubit na iyon (halimbawa, $XY = iZ$), at hindi na kakatawanin ng relaxed Hamiltonian ang interaction nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The assignment of variables to qubits therefore determines both the number of qubits and the quality of the relaxation, and SQOA Solver designs this assignment in its preprocessing.\n"
"- **Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD).** The quantum computer first prepares a quantum state that overlaps with low-energy states of the relaxed Hamiltonian and then samples bitstrings from it. A classical computer projects the relaxed Hamiltonian onto the subspace spanned by the sampled bitstrings and diagonalizes it to approximate the ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kaya ang pagtatalaga ng mga variable sa mga qubit ang nagtatakda ng bilang ng qubit at ng kalidad ng relaxation, at dinidisenyo ng SQOA Solver ang pagtatalagang ito sa preprocessing nito.\n"
"- **Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD).** Naghahanda muna ang quantum computer ng quantum state na may overlap sa mga low-energy state ng relaxed Hamiltonian, at pagkatapos ay nag-sample ng mga bitstring mula rito. Ipino-project ng classical computer ang relaxed Hamiltonian sa subspace na sakop ng mga na-sample na bitstring at dina-diagonalize ito para tantiyahin ang ground state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Because the relaxed Hamiltonian is non-diagonal, the diagonalization combines the sampled bitstrings into a superposition. With a diagonal Ising Hamiltonian, every bitstring is already an eigenstate, and the diagonalization would only select the best sample. The same approach has been applied to large-scale problems in quantum chemistry.\n"
msgstr "  Dahil non-diagonal ang relaxed Hamiltonian, pinagsasama ng diagonalization ang mga na-sample na bitstring sa isang superposition. Sa diagonal na Ising Hamiltonian, eigenstate na ang bawat bitstring, at pipiliin lang ng diagonalization ang pinakamahusay na sample. Ang parehong approach ay naipatupad na sa malalaking problema sa quantum chemistry.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The approximate ground state obtained by SQD does not directly correspond to a classical solution of the original problem, so the classical solution must be decoded from it. Because this state is computed on a classical computer, the decoding, called rounding, is classical postprocessing. SQOA Solver uses decoding techniques designed to obtain better classical solutions heuristically.\n"
msgstr "Ang tinatayang ground state na nakuha ng SQD ay hindi direktang tumutugma sa isang classical na solusyon ng orihinal na problema, kaya kailangang i-decode mula rito ang classical na solusyon. Dahil kinukuwenta ang state na ito sa isang classical computer, ang decoding, na tinatawag na rounding, ay classical postprocessing. Gumagamit ang SQOA Solver ng mga decoding technique na idinisenyo para heuristic na makakuha ng mas magagandang classical na solusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following table compares SQOA with QAOA, a common variational approach to the same class of problems.\n"
msgstr "Inihahambing ng sumusunod na table ang SQOA sa QAOA, isang karaniwang variational approach para sa parehong klase ng mga problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| &nbsp; | QAOA | SQOA |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Qubits for $n$ binary variables | $n$ | One qubit holds up to three of the variables. The exact number depends on the problem structure |\n"
"| Use of the QPU | Repeatedly estimates the energy of parameterized circuits inside a classical optimization loop | Only samples bitstrings. No circuit parameters are trained on the QPU |\n"
"| From samples to a solution | Selects the best measured bitstring | Diagonalizes the relaxed Hamiltonian in the sampled subspace on a classical computer and rounds the resulting state |\n"
msgstr ""
"| &nbsp; | QAOA | SQOA |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Mga qubit para sa $n$ binary variable | $n$ | Isang qubit ang may hawak ng hanggang tatlong variable. Nakadepende sa istruktura ng problema ang eksaktong bilang |\n"
"| Paggamit ng QPU | Paulit-ulit na tinatantiya ang energy ng mga parameterized circuit sa loob ng classical optimization loop | Nag-sample lang ng mga bitstring. Walang circuit parameter na tine-train sa QPU |\n"
"| Mula sa mga sample hanggang sa solusyon | Pinipili ang pinakamahusay na nasukat na bitstring | Dina-diagonalize ang relaxed Hamiltonian sa na-sample na subspace sa isang classical computer at nire-round ang nagresultang state |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Around SQOA-QR, SQOA Solver adds classical processing. Its preprocessing fixes variables whose optimal values can be determined in advance and designs the assignment of variables to qubits. Its postprocessing refines the rounded solution with a local search, which you can turn off with `postprocessing_level=0`.\n"
msgstr "Sa paligid ng SQOA-QR, nagdaragdag ang SQOA Solver ng classical processing. Inaayos ng preprocessing nito ang mga variable na ang optimal na halaga ay matutukoy nang maaga at dinidisenyo ang pagtatalaga ng mga variable sa mga qubit. Pinipino ng postprocessing nito ang na-round na solusyon gamit ang local search, na puwede mong i-off gamit ang `postprocessing_level=0`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Mga benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"  Performance can depend on both the problem instance and subsequent processing steps. In some cases, classical samples and quantum-generated samples might achieve similar final solution quality after equivalent postprocessing. Evaluation should therefore consider the complete optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"  Ang performance ay puwedeng depende sa problem instance at sa mga sumunod na processing step. Sa ilang kaso, ang mga classical na sample at quantum-generated na sample ay puwedeng makakuha ng magkatulad na kalidad ng huling solusyon pagkatapos ng katumbas na postprocessing. Kaya dapat isaalang-alang sa pagsusuri ang buong optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following benchmark metrics provide a general indication of solution quality, qubit compression, and execution time across selected problem sizes and structures. The table lists a selection of [Maximum Independent Set instances](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) from the Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB) and two 3-regular MaxCut instances. You can load the QOBLIB instances as `ommx.v1.Instance` objects, together with their optimal solutions, by using the [ommx-quantum-benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/) package.\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang mga sumusunod na benchmark metric ng pangkalahatang indikasyon ng kalidad ng solusyon, qubit compression, at execution time sa mga piling laki at istruktura ng problema. Inililista ng table ang ilang piling [Maximum Independent Set instance](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) mula sa Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB) at dalawang 3-regular MaxCut instance. Puwede mong i-load ang mga QOBLIB instance bilang mga `ommx.v1.Instance` object, kasama ang kanilang mga optimal na solusyon, gamit ang package na [ommx-quantum-benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each instance was run 10 times on an IBM Heron r2 processor. `Number of qubits` counts the qubits actually used on hardware after preprocessing and QRAC encoding. The compression ratio is instance-dependent. `Approximation ratio` (AR) reports the quality of the best solution found over the 10 runs:\n"
msgstr "Bawat instance ay pinatakbo nang 10 beses sa isang IBM Heron r2 processor. Binibilang ng `Number of qubits` ang mga qubit na aktuwal na ginamit sa hardware pagkatapos ng preprocessing at QRAC encoding. Nakadepende sa instance ang compression ratio. Iniuulat ng `Approximation ratio` (AR) ang kalidad ng pinakamahusay na solusyong nahanap sa loob ng 10 run:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{AR} = \\frac{C_{\\textrm{best}}}{C_{\\textrm{opt}}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{AR} = \\frac{C_{\\textrm{best}}}{C_{\\textrm{opt}}},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $C_{\\textrm{best}}$ is the best objective value found and $C_{\\textrm{opt}}$ is the known optimal objective value. All instances are maximization problems with a positive optimal value, so AR is at most 100%, and 100% in the `Approximation ratio` column indicates that the solver found an optimal solution. `Total time` is the average combined QPU and CPU time per run. `QPU time` is the average IBM Quantum Compute usage per run.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $C_{\\textrm{best}}$ ay ang pinakamahusay na objective value na nahanap at ang $C_{\\textrm{opt}}$ ay ang kilalang optimal na objective value. Lahat ng instance ay maximization problem na may positibong optimal value, kaya ang AR ay hindi lalampas sa 100%, at ang 100% sa column na `Approximation ratio` ay nangangahulugang nakahanap ang solver ng optimal na solusyon. Ang `Total time` ay ang average na pinagsamang QPU at CPU time bawat run. Ang `QPU time` ay ang average na paggamit ng IBM Quantum Compute bawat run.\n"

